#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124269 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84947238-f446-5261-8ecd-ee263f64e04f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given the Matrix Relative to Two Bases"}] :question/id #uuid "e9539818-ad55-5bb3-8c5d-5b85303f9e6d" :question/math-academy-id "e-5521" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/7d82125089d15dada1be4f8d6669b5e125da921019b3a9d27376353dcf59a090.png)\n\nSuppose $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C}$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the linear map $\\mathbf{T}:V \\rightarrow W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in V$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are shown above. Find $[\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{x})]_{\\mathcal{C}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124270 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Given With Respect to the Standard Basis Under a Linear Map"}] :question/id #uuid "8a371b65-8c57-5d10-88aa-2d4928fb028c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5522" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/8caf13cdbf21ddfb1a121ede6ec0c21da155065905547bbd86b0e52cd57141da.png)\n\nConsider the basis $\\mathcal{B}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ (shown above) and a basis $\\mathcal{C}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\nThe matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the linear map $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^3$ relative to these bases, and the vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^2,$ are also given. Find $[\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{x})]_{\\mathcal{C}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}},$ the coordinates of $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}.$ So, let\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/a5b6f5f41dffd99a885bb872eac6f1e6a24bd604b360256194a0bf16b32ef381.png)\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -18\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/862742d57ad0ae4b56d6f345d825313bebf0d712f9c59ea1ed8b55d0a2eea22e.png)\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124333 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f1e542-f0a2-54ea-ba7f-0a9928415907" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Using the Definition"}] :question/id #uuid "01b46867-ba6d-5085-9543-b77ded581194" :question/math-academy-id "e-8604" :question/problem "Suppose $\\mathbf{T} : V \\rightarrow W$ is a linear map and $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1,\\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3 \\}$ and $\\mathcal{C} = \\{ \\mathbf{c}_1,\\mathbf{c}_2 \\}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. Find the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the map $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1)=-3\\mathbf{c}_1+5\\mathbf{c}_2,\\quad$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2)=\\mathbf{c}_2-2\\mathbf{c}_1\\quad$ and $\\quad\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)=\\mathbf{c}_1+5\\mathbf{c}_2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the images of vectors in $\\mathcal{B}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C} \\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})=-3{c}_{1}+5{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2})={c}_{2}-2{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{3})={c}_{1}+5{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1),$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2)$ and $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/215cd69925ccfeab3ccb20874b7cdc2d837b99f33d8112f95fa5d2b646a27d40.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124334 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Given One Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "3d6b0aec-c282-581e-ae4a-560654d80e3b" :question/math-academy-id "e-8605" :question/problem "Consider the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3\\}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/7c123e6f7d842a8e86e4c99826d25df070982514960752a25481a9f3f046cc1b.png)\n\nFind the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the map $\\mathbf{T}:V \\to \\mathbb{R}^2$ relative to these bases if \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/9a469219c661453d7891935b2ef0a32bff972bcf903d641ca7e31b7bec26369a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1),$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2),$ and $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_i)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ for each $i=1,2,3.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/9d774b5bd79f14bc31e88a649fcb2a682d94ae3dd8acde5e25f52369c136e11e.png)\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 1 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -8 & 8\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 11 & -29 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -8 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C} \\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/778f179c4681bcdcc5a64bcd128d946a272fa869289d2c2e542df75ad05850b6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354366 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f1e542-f0a2-54ea-ba7f-0a9928415907" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0594c0af-6e6c-51aa-9cce-b3e6554aa20f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354368} {:answer/id #uuid "82eb51a0-cd2d-5ea7-b53e-01add5dbfd70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354369} {:answer/id #uuid "99b8ec31-ae1b-5c00-b85b-257e1424be3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354370} {:answer/id #uuid "796d939c-7e4b-5245-b0a3-70aa65d6b486" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354371} {:answer/id #uuid "b9782f89-b4e0-5847-93ac-9f45a11e8047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9782f89-b4e0-5847-93ac-9f45a11e8047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354372} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f06fbed-7e24-51d4-a2b8-282fc1d41ca6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90c70be1-8528-53a4-ba22-d67c27b7a631" :question/math-academy-id "q-140430" :question/problem "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Given One Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b779c74-6f76-5eb0-81c3-37d002687185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & -8 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354375} {:answer/id #uuid "a178be3c-a07f-529a-984a-d3103bb73369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354376} {:answer/id #uuid "c4d44ae6-e9d7-547a-b062-87f77aef76da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354377} {:answer/id #uuid "31377a3b-29e5-59ac-b6c3-61e4d6a980ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354378} {:answer/id #uuid "7c84edd3-624a-5ccf-a2e7-129048e9bde7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4d44ae6-e9d7-547a-b062-87f77aef76da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354377} :answer-field/id #uuid "77f5f3d0-7076-51ad-bb82-2b05b0ae1d1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c5b8550-93bd-5bca-bdbb-d5d6c011cb4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-140441" :question/problem "Consider the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ given by\n\n$$\nC={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T:V\\to {R}^{2}$ relative to these bases if \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354380 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84947238-f446-5261-8ecd-ee263f64e04f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given the Matrix Relative to Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b78b77f2-a4be-5f64-a850-8a9871ebbb49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -24 \\\\ -25\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354382} {:answer/id #uuid "489db10b-6898-5aa3-b1bd-8caf51b4ab13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354383} {:answer/id #uuid "08ecba04-211b-569b-a4df-bfba1f0e7ad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}25 \\\\ -24 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354384} {:answer/id #uuid "05e0f336-b731-540f-9777-3f179211b70a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}27 \\\\ 24 \\\\ -25\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354385} {:answer/id #uuid "25bf75fd-6e3d-54ba-b828-7ce3260e44d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ -27 \\\\ -25\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b78b77f2-a4be-5f64-a850-8a9871ebbb49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -24 \\\\ -25\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354382} :answer-field/id #uuid "5531d7e1-56b5-5917-8b31-07290e2a4f98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59fd0156-bcfb-5880-8b9a-95479297119c" :question/math-academy-id "q-140445" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -24 \\\\ -25\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354387 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Given With Respect to the Standard Basis Under a Linear Map"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ca59c40-b575-5fb8-859b-a5d4adc494bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 76 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354389} {:answer/id #uuid "83a05bf5-09e3-5cf6-9a96-e23b3e2e6af1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354390} {:answer/id #uuid "154bf734-4b6e-53dc-b46e-1652fe7adfd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354391} {:answer/id #uuid "481fdeb6-5f97-5658-8f34-864e77552c15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354392} {:answer/id #uuid "dfe8b6e5-bcea-5457-9d87-891bb6cf5360" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "154bf734-4b6e-53dc-b46e-1652fe7adfd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354391} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9ec63fa-aed8-5cd9-acf8-5502688e3186" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b32c830-750d-503e-9a1d-be23af443696" :question/math-academy-id "q-140446" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=-15 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 & -15 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 30\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 30\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 15\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354394 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f1e542-f0a2-54ea-ba7f-0a9928415907" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cf23380-5124-541f-b824-371e7d09e0e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354396} {:answer/id #uuid "787e23b4-ed9a-5ee2-93a1-1ae7597511ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354397} {:answer/id #uuid "66f71da7-7ea1-5537-bab8-0e862e253953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354398} {:answer/id #uuid "6e0fc3b5-6af8-5593-b89c-2bf45fd9ffed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354399} {:answer/id #uuid "2af2a4ec-ec75-5126-a936-b2cfa22ceabb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "787e23b4-ed9a-5ee2-93a1-1ae7597511ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354397} :answer-field/id #uuid "71f77607-7757-5ace-82d8-ef77977a9434" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354395}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a011b429-e2b6-51b5-aadf-3e1768c757ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-38528" :question/problem "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\,$ $T({b}_{1})={c}_{1}-{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=2{c}_{2}-{c}_{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the images of vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})={c}_{1}-{c}_{2}+{c}_{3} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2})=2{c}_{2}-{c}_{3} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and  $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125043 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f1e542-f0a2-54ea-ba7f-0a9928415907" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76713fa3-80e9-5e2d-b849-00bbfbc05e4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354402} {:answer/id #uuid "b66cbc25-a66a-53fb-b262-ae31062defcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354403} {:answer/id #uuid "913d6e26-2da1-5e72-80e6-fedcfbd52bab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354404} {:answer/id #uuid "27a36ffe-eef6-5e95-baf7-31366b9ffcc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 \\\\ -7 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354405} {:answer/id #uuid "7320f221-1bff-5e25-99d6-eab4ab640860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76713fa3-80e9-5e2d-b849-00bbfbc05e4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354402} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c41ddc7-6cdb-5fa6-ad78-123d0d2d32b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a7a7dfc1-b352-5fd9-84db-53ec5b318168" :question/math-academy-id "q-38529" :question/problem "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\,$ $T({b}_{1})=-2{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2}-2{c}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=3{c}_{2}-7{c}_{3}+{c}_{1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the images of vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})=-2{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2}-2{c}_{3} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2})=3{c}_{2}-7{c}_{3}+{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and  $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125044 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f1e542-f0a2-54ea-ba7f-0a9928415907" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bb78148-c648-5271-8c63-41205da64cae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354408} {:answer/id #uuid "d63416bc-03d0-5bd5-9cc8-6c2db63bd03a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354409} {:answer/id #uuid "f1cf43ae-5329-50a8-aaad-f7a4be2de149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354410} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e00d25-2820-5ef9-9572-a2e5d8114083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354411} {:answer/id #uuid "93988b8f-89b8-5b98-a50f-84edbcd95e1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bb78148-c648-5271-8c63-41205da64cae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354408} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa3af861-e22e-59e2-a7fc-f9d341fd5470" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f9af258-e8a2-56a9-9f94-0fa33495c61f" :question/math-academy-id "q-38530" :question/problem "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84947238-f446-5261-8ecd-ee263f64e04f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given the Matrix Relative to Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ca43dbc-4220-51d2-bca7-9fa2cd083dd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}21 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354415} {:answer/id #uuid "e20aecab-8828-5491-8c0f-98d22f418edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354416} {:answer/id #uuid "9286fd96-b85e-59e7-a1fb-3cad8a3ed53e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354417} {:answer/id #uuid "d8bffcfd-0956-5037-83cd-5dff40fc6de1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354418} {:answer/id #uuid "5d009b95-3c28-52ad-a531-66a793ee5b50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 21\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d009b95-3c28-52ad-a531-66a793ee5b50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 21\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354419} :answer-field/id #uuid "1347db9a-395a-5838-b5de-55b52622ea2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354414}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c934808-753e-50b9-9ad5-810e3e2b7ce4" :question/math-academy-id "q-38865" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 21\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354420 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f1e542-f0a2-54ea-ba7f-0a9928415907" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80f8d4b4-dee8-58fe-9ca1-3d2fbd510009" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354422} {:answer/id #uuid "0cfd86f2-28e9-57ec-90e0-34fdfe8652ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -3 \\\\ -8 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354423} {:answer/id #uuid "09bfa9c7-7638-5ffc-9927-37ea7b08d460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 8 \\\\ 6 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354424} {:answer/id #uuid "d39e123f-3723-5064-a3bc-c19090ffd8e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354425} {:answer/id #uuid "0b935ecc-1661-5ae8-b642-7b7d32329c9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b935ecc-1661-5ae8-b642-7b7d32329c9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354426} :answer-field/id #uuid "737d94d7-0dc7-5be2-871d-557b1534acea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "35486caf-b9d3-549e-b613-897d0cbc49da" :question/math-academy-id "q-38866" :question/problem "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84947238-f446-5261-8ecd-ee263f64e04f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given the Matrix Relative to Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42ec5ef5-3226-5721-bb74-c65a1194a061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-26 \\\\ 22\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354429} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a2102d-08e6-579e-9402-cc12c2ab0475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-22 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354430} {:answer/id #uuid "e4c4c9a8-9102-5da1-b34c-ab778affe9c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354431} {:answer/id #uuid "170b229a-691e-5ba2-b8a1-035eb1f41d65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354432} {:answer/id #uuid "ac1eba87-f597-5ed5-9fd7-d368125b430f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2a2102d-08e6-579e-9402-cc12c2ab0475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-22 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354430} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d62e9e1-67b4-596a-9224-cd873653b705" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29435b44-7a2b-5c1e-b63f-b6b051a05f5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-38867" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-22 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Given One Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e8da535-ec87-5ea5-826b-b4bec36b95ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -4 & -10 \\\\ -20 & 7 & 27\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354436} {:answer/id #uuid "d6201a8c-31fd-5d45-a6d7-516284466364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -20 & -4 \\\\ 27 & 10 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354437} {:answer/id #uuid "5e800eba-550a-59ca-af39-1c68062c95ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -20 & 27 \\\\ -4 & 7 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354438} {:answer/id #uuid "01f2d3bf-6dfc-543a-9f3a-13351e096fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & 7 & 27 \\\\ -10 & -20 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354439} {:answer/id #uuid "f571af07-7e56-5cd7-9e3c-76f6e47dc738" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -10 & 4 \\\\ 28 & 10 & -20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e800eba-550a-59ca-af39-1c68062c95ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -20 & 27 \\\\ -4 & 7 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354438} :answer-field/id #uuid "11272ddf-1648-54f4-9700-b8cf300821a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c34f2815-0a56-5b00-9bb6-d7163a1afbc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-97546" :question/problem "Consider the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ given by\n\n$$\nC={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T:V\\to {R}^{2}$ relative to these bases if \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{3})=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2,3.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) & T({b}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 2 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 7 & -10\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 10 & -20 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 7 & -10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}10 & -20 & 27 \\\\ -4 & 7 & -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354441 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Given One Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bb0e4b0-fd1f-5010-9b47-509e2952f52c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354443} {:answer/id #uuid "a7eeb636-7373-5639-a48b-91b4f1f6f961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354444} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e6d1cb-14b5-5912-838c-c051cd60e4b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354445} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f30ee3-82f9-5055-84fb-9ffc910f3403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354446} {:answer/id #uuid "7c4af7a1-c245-535d-848f-1168aaabe100" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7eeb636-7373-5639-a48b-91b4f1f6f961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354444} :answer-field/id #uuid "01fb7a34-82a4-5869-b408-6b57b31cbb69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354442}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ad57989-7a79-5aa3-aa45-200ce4a5483e" :question/math-academy-id "q-97547" :question/problem "Consider the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ given by\n\n$$\nC={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T:V\\to {R}^{2}$ relative to these bases if \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{3})=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2,3.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) & T({b}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -5 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Given One Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99daaac5-c2f8-575a-8bba-9157131e29d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354450} {:answer/id #uuid "80d8a130-e4bf-5365-a759-4ca40e313501" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354451} {:answer/id #uuid "2aece9b3-d85b-5667-af2c-bf28eb973a36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354452} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c68aa0-d239-5bd1-bea9-59ba078bf6e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354453} {:answer/id #uuid "f54f733a-06f1-57d3-9abe-024a54762a03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5c68aa0-d239-5bd1-bea9-59ba078bf6e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354453} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff1a9977-de1c-5cf0-a9ab-a7a55e5ff32d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6ab6a3b9-40b4-5b5f-8edf-85f76fb14b73" :question/math-academy-id "q-97549" :question/problem "Consider the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ given by\n\n$$\nC={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T:V\\to {R}^{2}$ relative to these bases if \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{3})=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2,3.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) & T({b}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Given One Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3ce5ea6-7f4f-532e-92b4-83e9e6116364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 12 \\\\ -3 & -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354457} {:answer/id #uuid "87fce1ef-36cd-5441-954f-790e0ffbecfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 & -3 \\\\ 12 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354458} {:answer/id #uuid "f9c7df68-ab29-50ec-921a-5951dabc6702" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 12 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354459} {:answer/id #uuid "817b0335-0543-50d5-8c8f-d2cefdb8c105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 & -11 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354460} {:answer/id #uuid "72f76471-7cc5-5d07-b8ff-5af3ed320d86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 12 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72f76471-7cc5-5d07-b8ff-5af3ed320d86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 12 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354461} :answer-field/id #uuid "2086c6ff-be93-540d-88e0-3990791946e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ee3204a4-be4d-5c58-b438-f3f6116c56d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-97572" :question/problem "Consider the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ given by\n\n$$\nC={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T:V\\to {R}^{2}$ relative to these bases if \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -5 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -11 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 12 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84947238-f446-5261-8ecd-ee263f64e04f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given the Matrix Relative to Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a33a3dc-11fb-5ea9-80dc-1b55af4729bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354464} {:answer/id #uuid "2a1761b3-a29b-5d84-aa71-3cd3a9228f54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354465} {:answer/id #uuid "6f07fde8-6086-5e2e-83c6-b5a10af7a4ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354466} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8520e8-e7bb-5fac-b3e7-0204aea8ac2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354467} {:answer/id #uuid "9a621fff-b714-5768-8612-4b6e871c8fb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a1761b3-a29b-5d84-aa71-3cd3a9228f54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354465} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e612b18-d53d-5954-8eae-f0f3dc54740a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "60898df4-cc3b-56d6-ad06-22874fbbe381" :question/math-academy-id "q-97576" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354469 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84947238-f446-5261-8ecd-ee263f64e04f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given the Matrix Relative to Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "081064af-3e0a-578c-93af-2079c3298952" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354471} {:answer/id #uuid "3a15d17b-f6d1-53a4-87fe-cdac33f555d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354472} {:answer/id #uuid "f41024b9-c000-53b9-9215-4f20b41b2777" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354473} {:answer/id #uuid "8c8333d3-2ec5-5285-826c-9a6a363e0753" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354474} {:answer/id #uuid "19c81ff5-4b1b-54da-baad-30c28b96bab8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f41024b9-c000-53b9-9215-4f20b41b2777" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354473} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ee44b5f-37e6-5398-867c-dcd4a69352b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "303d0a3a-b3af-56a9-8727-cf349c848e46" :question/math-academy-id "q-97579" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}9 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Given With Respect to the Standard Basis Under a Linear Map"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e127cb80-0d0c-5c09-bd43-3823e3e330f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354478} {:answer/id #uuid "c08e2385-b8f9-54e6-b415-a2d014aa819a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354479} {:answer/id #uuid "05d4cb5d-df13-53c1-92fa-e9a162c673ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354480} {:answer/id #uuid "5f3b1c53-7659-5b55-a2d1-22f6bf38ffcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354481} {:answer/id #uuid "8570f05d-0e31-5c77-bc90-c91c0bd043f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f3b1c53-7659-5b55-a2d1-22f6bf38ffcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354481} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe057ce2-70b5-5f38-8543-580eca972165" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "473ad29f-d952-5261-9293-cd15e4622b57" :question/math-academy-id "q-97583" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354483 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Given With Respect to the Standard Basis Under a Linear Map"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58f62d00-5c59-59e6-9f02-b0290bb8035a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/