$x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}=-4 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125169 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Given With Respect to the Standard Basis Under a Linear Map"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdbc00ca-6368-5448-b022-68cb649556d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124037} {:answer/id #uuid "d27e46cd-6e4b-5b9a-831b-d6686a4c49c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/va