lative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354490 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Given With Respect to the Standard Basis Under a Linear Map"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f2be7d8-1087-51de-ba3d-497da290d3aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354492} {:answer/id #uuid "066d82f9-8b3e-5206-92c1-af8a908d4082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354493} {:answer/id #uuid "e062d0a7-6e98-52c9-82a2-53a3795d7edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354494} {:answer/id #uuid "9237ea21-9